# Only secrets live here. Store domains live in .syncifyrc.json
# (from.store / to.store) — see that file, written by `syncify init`.
#
# Two ways to authenticate each store — use ONE of them per store, not both.
# See README.md "Getting the Production/Dev token" for full setup steps.

# --- Option A: legacy custom app (static token) ---
# Only works if the custom app was created before 2026-01-01 — Shopify no
# longer allows creating new legacy custom apps as of that date. Existing
# ones keep working fine.
# Production store — READ-ONLY custom app token. Grant it ONLY
# read_products, read_online_store_pages, read_discounts, read_metaobjects,
# read_metaobject_definitions, read_files scopes (no write_* scopes; shop
# and product metafields need no scope at all — see README). This is the
# primary safety mechanism: even if syncify's logic ever pointed the wrong
# direction, this token cannot write.
SHOPIFY_PROD_TOKEN=shpat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Dev store — read-write custom app token.
SHOPIFY_DEV_TOKEN=shpat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --- Option B: Dev Dashboard app (Client ID + secret) ---
# Required for any app created on or after 2026-01-01. syncify exchanges
# these for a short-lived Admin API token itself at the start of each run —
# leave SHOPIFY_PROD_TOKEN/SHOPIFY_DEV_TOKEN above unset (or delete them) if
# using this instead.
# SHOPIFY_PROD_CLIENT_ID=
# SHOPIFY_PROD_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SHOPIFY_DEV_CLIENT_ID=
# SHOPIFY_DEV_CLIENT_SECRET=
